  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v4.9.9: Three browser-backend fixes + a new async copy API, batched from local.1/2/3. (1) WebGPU scalar-slot drift: kernels with body-struct params followed by trailing scalars emitted the scalars at the wrong `_scalar_params` slots (header and binding setup disagreed), silently corrupting those scalars; both sides now agree. Root cause of the ML Phase 2 TensorView /depth flat-blue regression. WebGPU sweep 606/0/7. (2) WebGL GPU→GPU CopyTo/CopyFrom read the stale CPU-side `_backingArray` instead of the worker's canonical post-kernel `entry.data`, producing all-zeros after a kernel Transform Feedback write; now routed through a worker-side `copyBuffer` message. WebGL sweep 484/0/144. (3) NEW backend-agnostic `CopyFromAsync` extension on `ArrayView<T>`, `ArrayView1D<T,TStride>`, `MemoryBuffer1D<T,TStride>` — mirrors sync `CopyFrom` and drains pending Wasm worker dispatches before the copy (no-op on other backends), closing the Blazor-WASM main-thread race where sync `CopyFrom` read `SharedArrayBuffer` mid-write. 14/14 across all 7 backend test classes. (4) Wasm barrier verdict: re-confirmed `memory.atomic.wait32/notify` dispatcher barriers still race on V8 (chromium#490434403 family) — pure spin stays; the gated, default-off `WasmBackend.UseWaitNotifyBarriers` re-test harness is retained for re-validation against a future V8 fix.",
